Z||000016||Lady Pegasus||11-28-2001||09:12 PM||||I would rather have an *******  for a dad then no dad at all.  I was 15 when my father was diagnosed with lung cancer, only it wasn't that simple.  It had gone undiagnosed for six months to a year, and when we finally did catch it, it was too late to do anything.  The cancer was in his central nervous sytem and then got into his blood stream.  Only seven weeks after he was diagosed (and only four days after his 41st birthday) he passed away.  Believe me, I would kill just to hear his voice, even if it's just to yell at me.  That's the first thing you forget.  I miss his laugh, I miss waking up to the smell of bacon and coffee in the morning.  I sometimes find myself walking down the hairspray isle in the grocery store and grabbing a can of what he used, just so I can remind myself of him.  It's been six years now, and the pain still hasn't gone away.  Not a day goes by that I don't think about him.  Believe me, you will NEVER realize what you have until it is gone.  I would give ANYTHING to get one more second with my father.  ||||reg||1
